  "backstory": "Born in 1990 in Tashkent, UZB. In the bustling streets of Tashkent, a young father-to-be at 26 years old is navigating the complexities of impending parenthood with a blend of warmth and quiet authority. He carries the weight of his own childhood, where his needs often took a backseat to those of others, leading him to believe that expressing his desires is a luxury reserved for the fortunate. His heart is filled with hopes for a better future for his baby, yet a simmering fear lurks beneath: that he may not be enough, that his child might feel the same neglect he did. As he prepares to welcome his new life, he is driven by a longing to offer love and security, even as he grapples with the struggle to assert his own needs. In a society steeped in collectivism, he clings to the belief that his child will thrive within the community, yet he is painfully aware of the fragility of trust, having witnessed the hardships of those around him. He approaches fatherhood with a mixture of hope and trepidation, determined to provide material support despite his own limited resources, and yearning to convey the unspoken message that his child is deeply wanted. As the mother prepares for the arrival of her baby in Tashkent, her heart is a jumble of fierce love and guarded apprehension. At 25, she embodies the spirit of an Enneagram Type 8, exuding a robust authority that both comforts and intimidates. Her warmth is tempered by a deep-seated fear of vulnerability; she believes that trust is a luxury she cannot afford. Despite her innate desire for connection, her experiences have taught her that betrayal lurks in the shadows, and she shields herself with a facade of stoicism. \n\nLiving in the bustling city, she hopes to provide a future filled with opportunities, yet she often feels the weight of their modest socioeconomic status, which makes her protective instincts flare. Her parenting style will likely be a blend of strict guidance and fierce loyalty, as she strives to cultivate resilience in her child while struggling internally with the fear of being let down. In this complex emotional landscape, she carries the hope that her baby will learn to navigate the world with strength, but her own unresolved feelings about trust will shape the environment into which this new life is born.",
